WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.730
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.000 --> 00:09.440
You said the Crow Club takes secret jobs and can solve any problem.

3
00:09.520 --> 00:10.400
Is that true or just an exaggeration?

4
00:11.000 --> 00:13.200
Tomorrow, a client will come to discuss a job with us.

5
00:13.280 --> 00:15.040
The client just wants you

6
00:15.120 --> 00:18.240
to negotiate with the ghost that's following him.

7
00:18.320 --> 00:20.600
I'm forming a band to make our debut.

8
00:20.680 --> 00:22.600
I want to invite you to join the band.

9
00:22.680 --> 00:24.240
I've decided.

10
00:24.320 --> 00:25.960
I'll use him as the model for the male lead in my novel.

11
00:26.560 --> 00:27.760
He's my client?

12
00:27.840 --> 00:29.360
I won't take a client like him.

13
00:29.440 --> 00:30.400
But for this…

14
00:30.480 --> 00:32.280
You're the only one who can help me.

15
00:32.360 --> 00:34.080
It's time for me to let the clients know

16
00:34.160 --> 00:35.920
whether you'll take the jobs.

17
00:52.120 --> 00:52.960
Why is it so tight?

18
00:53.760 --> 00:55.400
You're really struggling, huh?

19
00:57.120 --> 00:58.120
Hey!

20
01:06.080 --> 01:08.560
EDITOR

21
02:28.120 --> 02:31.120
If you don't want to do it, why take the job?

22
02:31.720 --> 02:33.280
Because I don't want to lose.

23
02:34.160 --> 02:36.000
If I don't take this job,

24
02:36.080 --> 02:38.000
Yoyeh will think that I…

25
02:38.080 --> 02:40.440
still haven't moved on from him.

26
02:40.520 --> 02:42.120
Well, have you really moved on?

27
02:47.520 --> 02:49.640
Anyone could guess in a situation like this.

28
02:50.640 --> 02:53.840
He's willing to work with the ex he hates again.

29
02:55.520 --> 02:56.640
Dear Vann.

30
02:57.360 --> 02:59.240
Just wait and see Tangmo.

31
03:00.080 --> 03:01.560
Old flames are bound to reignite.

32
03:08.600 --> 03:10.760
If you don't like it, just turn him down.

33
03:11.320 --> 03:13.240
Why make it so complicated?

34
03:13.800 --> 03:16.240
If I don't want to do it, I say no.

35
03:16.320 --> 03:17.480
What's so hard about that?

36
03:18.080 --> 03:19.760
You never care about anything.

37
03:19.840 --> 03:21.200
Of course you'd say that.

38
03:21.280 --> 03:22.560
True.

39
03:22.640 --> 03:23.880
If Talay ever took a job,

40
03:24.480 --> 03:26.080
the sun would rise in the west.

41
03:29.240 --> 03:30.840
Vann, your job starts today.

42
03:31.600 --> 03:32.560
Why haven't you left yet?

43
03:33.080 --> 03:34.640
Come on.

44
03:34.720 --> 03:36.960
You only kick me out because I'm the youngest.

45
03:37.040 --> 03:40.360
When the others are loud, you never say anything to them.

46
03:40.440 --> 03:42.120
I say it in my head, but no one hears it.

47
03:44.840 --> 03:48.080
So, did you get a job, Phatee?

48
03:54.840 --> 03:57.160
If we don't expect anything, we won't be disappointed.

49
03:57.240 --> 03:58.960
Whatever we ask him,

50
03:59.040 --> 04:01.160
we never get an answer.

51
04:03.440 --> 04:04.360
What about you?

52
04:04.960 --> 04:06.760
Can you handle a ghost-hunting job like this?

53
04:06.840 --> 04:08.200
I took the job,

54
04:08.280 --> 04:09.800
so I have to solve the problem for my client.

55
04:10.680 --> 04:12.680
I don't care what I have to do.

56
04:12.760 --> 04:13.880
But one thing's for sure,

57
04:13.960 --> 04:15.320
I'm going to finish the job.

58
04:18.320 --> 04:19.760
That one million baht…

59
04:21.560 --> 04:23.200
has to be mine.

60
04:32.520 --> 04:35.080
Thank you for taking this job.

61
04:36.880 --> 04:37.920
No problem.

62
04:38.520 --> 04:40.040
I just feel sorry for you.

63
04:41.080 --> 04:42.400
I can't stand seeing anyone in trouble.

64
04:43.760 --> 04:45.560
And you said you'd pay me one million.

65
04:46.640 --> 04:48.080
You really have the money to pay me, right?

66
04:49.320 --> 04:50.400
Wait a moment.

67
05:03.320 --> 05:04.400
Shit.

68
05:04.480 --> 05:06.640
Having eight figures in your account…

69
05:06.720 --> 05:07.920
What does that even feel like?

70
05:09.560 --> 05:11.520
No matter how much money I have,

71
05:11.600 --> 05:13.200
I won't be happy

72
05:13.960 --> 05:15.880
if a ghost keeps haunting me like this.

73
05:15.960 --> 05:18.080
If you have this much money,

74
05:18.160 --> 05:19.560
why don't you move away from the ghost?

75
05:19.640 --> 05:22.840
Move to Switzerland or Korea.

76
05:22.920 --> 05:24.920
A ghost can't get through immigration.

77
05:25.520 --> 05:27.080
The ghost isn't haunting the house,

78
05:27.160 --> 05:28.800
and it isn't following me either.

79
05:28.880 --> 05:31.240
It only appears when I'm with my boyfriend.

80
05:31.320 --> 05:33.120
I never know when it'll show up.

81
05:33.200 --> 05:34.760
There's no pattern at all.

82
05:34.840 --> 05:37.000
And it can go anywhere.

83
05:37.080 --> 05:38.400
You said it couldn't get through immigration?

84
05:39.160 --> 05:40.800
So where am I supposed to run?

85
05:42.920 --> 05:44.360
Okay.

86
05:44.440 --> 05:45.680
If that's really the case,

87
05:45.760 --> 05:48.600
I'll make that ghost run for its life.

88
05:48.680 --> 05:50.160
But the thing is,

89
05:50.240 --> 05:51.800
for the ghost to appear,

90
05:51.880 --> 05:54.400
you'd have to be my boyfriend first.

91
05:55.000 --> 05:57.400
Wait, so I'm not just negotiating with the ghost?

92
05:57.480 --> 05:59.560
I have to pretend to be your boyfriend to fool it too?

93
05:59.640 --> 06:01.640
We'll trick it into coming out first,

94
06:01.720 --> 06:03.560
then you can chase it away.

95
06:04.840 --> 06:06.600
Linda told me

96
06:06.680 --> 06:08.480
you often work as a fake boyfriend.

97
06:08.560 --> 06:11.200
This is just another job. Right?

98
06:11.800 --> 06:13.400
But are you sure

99
06:13.480 --> 06:15.640
if we put on an act,

100
06:15.720 --> 06:17.960
the ghost will be dumb enough to believe us and come out?

101
06:20.320 --> 06:21.960
You just have to make it convincing enough

102
06:22.040 --> 06:23.240
for it to believe us.

103
06:29.880 --> 06:31.960
I've connected every device to our room's Wi-Fi.

104
06:32.720 --> 06:35.640
And I'm syncing the data to the cloud server in real time.

105
06:36.560 --> 06:38.400
If any energy wave interferes,

106
06:38.480 --> 06:40.120
the system will alert us immediately.

107
06:40.880 --> 06:42.200
Wow.

108
06:42.280 --> 06:43.400
You look really nerdy.

109
06:43.480 --> 06:44.640
That's not all.

110
06:53.600 --> 06:55.840
This measures physiological responses.

111
06:56.920 --> 06:58.480
I'll use you as a warning radar.

112
06:59.400 --> 07:01.080
When this pen goes off,

113
07:01.160 --> 07:02.240
it means the ghost is here.

114
07:02.920 --> 07:04.560
So I'll be ready to curse it out.

115
07:05.160 --> 07:06.880
Unbutton your shirt a little.

116
07:06.960 --> 07:08.920
Just two buttons.

117
07:09.000 --> 07:10.040
What?

118
07:10.640 --> 07:12.520
Just hurry up and do it. Don't ask questions.

119
07:59.760 --> 08:00.800
You're all set.

120
08:06.600 --> 08:08.040
The graph's spiking this much.

121
08:10.040 --> 08:12.720
Does… Does it mean the ghost is here?

122
08:15.240 --> 08:16.720
This thing must be sensitive.

123
08:17.600 --> 08:18.600
Show me.

124
08:18.680 --> 08:20.120
Where did you last see it?

125
08:23.720 --> 08:24.560
Here.

126
08:26.920 --> 08:28.840
-Here? -Yeah.

127
08:29.800 --> 08:31.160
What were you doing then?

128
08:35.320 --> 08:36.799
At the time, I…

129
08:36.880 --> 08:38.520
I was kissing my boyfriend.

130
08:39.559 --> 08:41.360
He was about to kiss me.

131
08:49.400 --> 08:50.360
Shit!

132
08:51.240 --> 08:53.400
Kan, where are you going?

133
08:53.480 --> 08:54.720
Enough, enough.

134
08:57.320 --> 08:58.360
What about before that?

135
08:58.960 --> 09:01.840
What else happens when the ghost appears?

136
09:01.920 --> 09:03.360
Tell me about it.

137
09:05.320 --> 09:06.760
Before that…

138
09:10.920 --> 09:13.160
-Get out! -Shit!

139
09:20.400 --> 09:21.480
What's wrong?

140
09:21.560 --> 09:22.920
Nothing's wrong.

141
09:27.320 --> 09:29.120
Why did you hit me on the head?

142
09:29.200 --> 09:30.720
I didn't.

143
09:32.040 --> 09:34.000
If it wasn't you, who else could it be?

144
09:34.880 --> 09:37.000
Don't bother me anymore.

145
09:37.080 --> 09:39.440
That's why I've never had a serious relationship.

146
09:39.520 --> 09:42.400
I've gone to see monks from many different places.

147
09:42.480 --> 09:45.120
I've made merit to atone for my karma. I've tried everything.

148
09:45.200 --> 09:46.560
This time, it'll definitely disappear.

149
09:46.640 --> 09:47.920
I'll make sure of it.

150
09:48.000 --> 09:49.920
I'm determined to finish this job.

151
09:51.000 --> 09:52.480
Because you feel sorry for me?

152
09:53.200 --> 09:55.240
No. I'm doing it for the money.

153
09:55.840 --> 09:57.600
I have a reason I need one million baht soon.

154
09:58.560 --> 10:00.840
So I'll need your cooperation as the client.

155
10:08.160 --> 10:10.760
We agreed to pretend to be a couple.

156
10:12.720 --> 10:13.760
Oh.

157
10:38.000 --> 10:39.480
If you're easily affected,

158
10:39.560 --> 10:41.200
these graphs won't be very accurate.

159
10:44.040 --> 10:45.640
You need to toughen up a little.

160
10:46.520 --> 10:47.640
Try taking a deep breath.

161
10:48.160 --> 10:50.080
Then sit and wait for the ghost to come haunt you.

162
10:53.880 --> 10:56.800
But I don't know if the ghost will come out.

163
10:59.320 --> 11:02.280
You said the ghost doesn't want you to have a partner, right?

164
11:02.360 --> 11:03.680
We just…

165
11:03.760 --> 11:04.960
We just provoke the ghost.

166
11:06.120 --> 11:07.120
What do I have to do?

167
11:25.840 --> 11:26.920
Put some effort into it.

168
11:28.120 --> 11:29.120
Again.

169
11:59.840 --> 12:01.440
Looks like it'll take quite a while.

170
12:03.440 --> 12:05.200
I'll probably have to move in here temporarily.

171
12:05.880 --> 12:07.120
Is that okay?

172
12:07.200 --> 12:08.640
Sure.

173
12:08.720 --> 12:10.080
When will you move in?

174
12:10.680 --> 12:11.720
Tonight works.

175
12:28.640 --> 12:30.840
I understand that we have to pretend to be a couple.

176
12:31.720 --> 12:34.440
But can bedtime count as a break?

177
12:51.560 --> 12:53.040
You keep moving closer to me.

178
12:53.120 --> 12:54.600
Are you a person or a worm?

179
12:54.680 --> 12:56.560
Move over.

180
13:01.560 --> 13:02.920
I'm a light sleeper.

181
13:03.000 --> 13:05.440
If anything touches me, I really can't sleep.

182
13:13.680 --> 13:15.120
This side is a you-free zone.

183
13:15.200 --> 13:18.120
If you cross over, I'll charge you ten thousand each time.

184
13:19.120 --> 13:20.440
I can actually afford that.

185
13:21.560 --> 13:23.040
You're really persistent.

186
13:24.480 --> 13:25.760
Good night.

187
13:44.960 --> 13:46.160
What happened?

188
13:46.240 --> 13:47.720
Is there a fire?

189
13:50.920 --> 13:53.680
It's time for our romance-to-lure-a-ghost mission.

190
13:53.760 --> 13:55.800
Hurry up and get up.

191
13:56.400 --> 13:58.280
Let me sleep for another ten minutes.

192
13:58.360 --> 13:59.840
No.

193
14:01.120 --> 14:02.440
Five minutes, then.

194
14:03.040 --> 14:05.360
Vann, didn't you say you wanted to finish this mission quickly?

195
14:05.440 --> 14:06.400
Come on.

196
14:06.920 --> 14:08.960
Wake up.

197
14:11.520 --> 14:12.520
Are you crazy?

198
14:12.600 --> 14:14.720
Who the hell wakes up to flirt this early?

199
14:14.800 --> 14:16.200
Me.

200
14:16.280 --> 14:17.760
Get out of bed.

201
14:18.480 --> 14:19.480
Come on.

202
14:19.560 --> 14:20.560
Vann, get out of bed.

203
14:30.200 --> 14:31.560
Vann.

204
14:31.640 --> 14:32.680
Vann.

205
14:34.160 --> 14:35.880
-Vann. -What?

206
14:35.960 --> 14:37.000
Is the ghost here?

207
14:37.080 --> 14:39.080
Come on, let's go running.

208
14:45.440 --> 14:46.960
Wait, wait.

209
14:52.200 --> 14:53.360
Are you okay?

210
15:02.520 --> 15:03.440
You don't have to.

211
15:09.360 --> 15:10.320
But…

212
15:10.400 --> 15:11.520
you can wipe it for me.

213
15:12.720 --> 15:13.880
Make it sweet.

214
15:14.640 --> 15:15.960
Okay, do it.

215
15:34.440 --> 15:35.640
Do you see anything?

216
15:37.040 --> 15:38.640
I don't.

217
15:50.120 --> 15:51.320
Vann, let's take a picture together.

218
15:56.280 --> 15:58.400
No matter how you look at it, we don't look like a couple.

219
15:59.160 --> 16:00.480
Don't you think?

220
16:01.240 --> 16:02.320
Yeah.

221
16:02.400 --> 16:04.320
Let's not do this activity anymore.

222
16:04.400 --> 16:05.640
It's not working.

223
16:08.760 --> 16:10.680
Vann, try this.

224
16:10.760 --> 16:12.120
The coffee here is good.

225
16:12.960 --> 16:14.040
No.

226
16:14.120 --> 16:15.720
If you want me to try it, go get a new straw.

227
16:16.320 --> 16:17.840
Come on, Vann.

228
16:17.920 --> 16:20.240
We're a couple, so we have to use the same straw.

229
16:22.640 --> 16:23.600
Just a little.

230
16:28.160 --> 16:29.680
So cute.

231
16:36.560 --> 16:38.640
How is this supposed to fool a ghost?

232
16:38.720 --> 16:40.240
You can't even fool a person with that.

233
16:40.840 --> 16:42.040
This is how you do it.

234
16:55.000 --> 16:56.960
Hey, why didn't you take the picture?

235
16:57.040 --> 16:58.960
-Okay. -Take another one.

236
17:22.240 --> 17:23.440
Where's the ghost?

237
17:25.400 --> 17:27.520
Maybe our acting still isn't convincing enough.

238
17:28.200 --> 17:29.080
I'm leaving.

239
17:35.000 --> 17:36.480
We've been together for hours.

240
17:37.040 --> 17:38.320
The ghost still hasn't shown up.

241
17:40.000 --> 17:43.240
Even a dog could tell we're not close.

242
17:43.840 --> 17:45.080
It's forced, Vann.

243
17:46.120 --> 17:47.400
Let me ask you seriously.

244
17:47.480 --> 17:49.800
Have you ever been in love?

245
17:51.320 --> 17:53.200
That's personal. Nothing to do with the job.

246
17:53.280 --> 17:54.320
Why are you asking?

247
17:54.400 --> 17:56.200
Of course it has to do with the job.

248
17:56.800 --> 17:58.840
We have to fool the ghost into thinking we're a couple.

249
17:58.920 --> 18:01.040
But you don't seem to understand love at all.

250
18:01.120 --> 18:02.600
So what's a good boyfriend supposed to be like?

251
18:03.320 --> 18:04.680
Do I have to remember your size?

252
18:05.360 --> 18:07.840
And when you forget condoms, do I have to rush out to buy them?

253
18:07.920 --> 18:10.000
You keep reminding me. I remember your size.

254
18:10.080 --> 18:11.240
Hey!

255
18:11.320 --> 18:12.760
Calm down.

256
18:20.440 --> 18:21.640
Hey.

257
18:21.720 --> 18:23.760
Are you that pervert from the elevator that day?

258
18:26.400 --> 18:27.600
Yes.

259
18:27.680 --> 18:29.000
That's me.

260
18:29.760 --> 18:31.080
But let me say something.

261
18:31.160 --> 18:33.400
In the end, no matter how much you indulge him,

262
18:33.480 --> 18:35.040
when he's in serious trouble,

263
18:35.120 --> 18:37.200
your boyfriend still leaves you, doesn't he?

264
18:37.280 --> 18:39.400
What do you know?

265
18:40.040 --> 18:42.320
You've never even had a boyfriend before.

266
18:43.200 --> 18:45.160
And now you're acting like you know everything?

267
18:46.520 --> 18:48.640
Hey. Don't be mad.

268
18:48.720 --> 18:51.000
If you're not ready to understand love,

269
18:51.080 --> 18:52.160
then don't say anything.

270
18:52.240 --> 18:53.920
I'm just going by theory.

271
18:54.000 --> 18:56.320
In theory, good love should be like this.

272
18:56.400 --> 18:58.880
Stop rambling about theories that don't fucking work.

273
18:58.960 --> 19:00.720
Because they don't work in practice.

274
19:02.360 --> 19:04.440
I think we should stop here for today.

275
19:04.520 --> 19:06.480
I need some time alone to think.

276
19:06.560 --> 19:07.760
Hey.

277
19:07.840 --> 19:09.880
Aren't you afraid of the ghost anymore?

278
19:09.960 --> 19:11.160
It's fine.

279
19:11.240 --> 19:13.600
If I'm alone, the ghost won't appear.

280
19:14.760 --> 19:17.360
Or maybe I'll have to fucking live alone like this forever.

281
19:19.040 --> 19:20.720
Hey, wait!

282
19:24.000 --> 19:26.960
He says he's not mad, but I think he clearly is.

283
19:31.000 --> 19:31.920
This is Nugget's new home.

284
19:34.880 --> 19:36.040
What is this?

285
19:36.880 --> 19:39.080
Egg cartons help diffuse sound waves

286
19:39.160 --> 19:41.320
and soak up noise so it doesn't leak out.

287
19:45.880 --> 19:47.200
That's amazing.

288
19:48.240 --> 19:50.680
It does keep the sound in,

289
19:50.760 --> 19:52.280
but I wonder…

290
19:53.640 --> 19:56.000
will it be able to breathe?

291
19:56.080 --> 19:59.520
Doesn't it look too cramped and stuffy?

292
20:00.200 --> 20:01.760
Hey,

293
20:02.320 --> 20:03.360
I think

294
20:04.880 --> 20:07.200
in theory, it might work.

295
20:07.280 --> 20:10.120
But in practice,

296
20:10.200 --> 20:11.680
I don't think it'll work.

297
20:11.760 --> 20:14.840
How would I know? I've never had one.

298
20:15.520 --> 20:16.520
Never had what?

299
20:16.600 --> 20:17.480
A boyf…

300
20:19.560 --> 20:21.280
I mean, I've never been a chick.

301
20:21.360 --> 20:22.800
I've never been a chick either.

302
20:22.880 --> 20:24.160
No one's ever been a chick.

303
20:25.600 --> 20:26.560
There you guys are.

304
20:26.640 --> 20:29.000
What are you doing? Reading cards again?

305
20:29.080 --> 20:31.240
Yeah, here.

306
20:31.320 --> 20:33.560
-What's this? -Don't touch it, Linda.

307
20:33.640 --> 20:35.000
This is my new product.

308
20:35.080 --> 20:36.120
Don't mess with it.

309
20:36.720 --> 20:37.960
You're that protective of it?

310
20:38.040 --> 20:40.600
And how's the job with Rakkhun going?

311
20:44.240 --> 20:45.400
Great.

312
20:46.160 --> 20:48.600
The chemistry between me and him is really good.

313
20:49.560 --> 20:52.400
I guarantee this job will be done ahead of schedule.

314
20:53.000 --> 20:56.440
It's good that you two have great chemistry.

315
20:56.520 --> 20:58.440
Because if you screw up this job,

316
20:58.520 --> 21:00.960
I guarantee you'll be a waiter here until you die.

317
21:01.720 --> 21:03.040
You probably won't make it to Japan.

318
21:16.840 --> 21:19.880
Vann, what are you doing?

319
21:27.680 --> 21:29.400
So basically,

320
21:30.080 --> 21:31.640
you told your client off,

321
21:31.720 --> 21:33.240
so he got upset.

322
21:33.320 --> 21:34.680
Then he just disappeared.

323
21:35.560 --> 21:36.840
Yeah.

324
21:36.920 --> 21:38.760
I just criticized him based on what I thought.

325
21:39.360 --> 21:41.360
But when I saw Nugget just now,

326
21:41.440 --> 21:42.680
I realized

327
21:42.760 --> 21:45.240
you can't rely on theory alone for things like this.

328
21:46.240 --> 21:47.760
If I don't experience it myself, I won't know.

329
21:48.480 --> 21:49.360
You're screwed.

330
21:49.960 --> 21:52.520
I think you should confess to Linda

331
21:52.600 --> 21:54.640
that your client ran away from you.

332
21:54.720 --> 21:56.640
-Go. -No.

333
21:56.720 --> 21:58.160
I don't want to give up.

334
21:58.760 --> 22:00.240
If you don't want to give up,

335
22:00.320 --> 22:02.160
you have to go apologize to him

336
22:02.240 --> 22:04.440
and tell him, "I was wrong."

337
22:05.120 --> 22:07.320
But he told me he wanted to be alone.

338
22:08.480 --> 22:10.760
Let me tell you something.

339
22:10.840 --> 22:13.400
When people are a couple and they're upset,

340
22:13.480 --> 22:16.440
they'll say, "I want to be alone."

341
22:16.520 --> 22:18.560
-But no one actually wants to be alone. -Yeah.

342
22:18.640 --> 22:21.000
And no one leaves their partner alone either.

343
22:21.080 --> 22:21.920
Except you.

344
22:23.280 --> 22:25.880
He's just my fake boyfriend.

345
22:35.800 --> 22:37.840
Guys. Rakkhun messaged me.

346
22:37.920 --> 22:40.600
You're screwed. I don't even need to read the cards to know.

347
22:40.680 --> 22:42.200
You're definitely getting fired. You're done for.

348
22:42.880 --> 22:44.280
Did he message you to fire you?

349
22:44.360 --> 22:47.480
Shit, that mouth of yours.

350
22:47.560 --> 22:48.440
‎RAKKHUN

351
22:48.520 --> 22:51.400
Vann. What are you doing?

352
22:54.240 --> 22:55.360
Guys.

353
22:56.120 --> 22:58.080
I survived. My job's not canceled yet.

354
22:58.680 --> 22:59.640
I'm off.

355
22:59.720 --> 23:01.640
My funds for Japan are waiting for me.

356
23:01.720 --> 23:03.360
I'm going.

357
23:10.360 --> 23:11.480
Why did you call me here?

358
23:11.560 --> 23:12.720
Are you going to fire me?

359
23:14.680 --> 23:15.640
No.

360
23:18.000 --> 23:19.800
You looked really angry with me earlier,

361
23:19.880 --> 23:21.520
so I thought you were going to fire me.

362
23:34.160 --> 23:35.160
It was my fault.

363
23:37.200 --> 23:38.880
I don't know what I was thinking then.

364
23:39.480 --> 23:42.280
Maybe I was angry because you hit a nerve about my exes.

365
23:43.360 --> 23:45.840
Because I know sometimes it wasn't really love.

366
23:47.040 --> 23:49.240
But I just want to have a good relationship

367
23:49.320 --> 23:50.760
like everyone else.

368
23:50.840 --> 23:51.920
-I just… -Enough.

369
23:53.640 --> 23:54.520
You don't have to say anything else.

370
23:55.720 --> 23:57.320
I'm the one who should apologize.

371
23:59.640 --> 24:01.960
I don't really know your happiness or your pain,

372
24:02.040 --> 24:04.480
yet I had the nerve to judge your life.

373
24:05.920 --> 24:07.840
I'm sorry I left you alone.

374
24:09.120 --> 24:10.080
Can we…

375
24:10.840 --> 24:11.880
Can we make up?

376
24:21.920 --> 24:23.120
So we're good now, right?

377
24:25.080 --> 24:26.160
We're good.

378
24:26.840 --> 24:29.360
From now on, I'm running the system for real.

379
24:30.920 --> 24:31.960
Vann.

380
24:33.480 --> 24:35.040
Thank you so much.

381
24:36.680 --> 24:37.800
Don't worry.

382
24:38.400 --> 24:40.480
Tomorrow, I'll take you on an organic-style date.

383
24:41.360 --> 24:43.120
I guarantee the ghost will come out.

384
24:51.200 --> 24:53.000
Come in a little more. You're almost there.

385
24:57.400 --> 24:59.240
You brought me for an ice bath?

386
24:59.320 --> 25:00.720
Yeah.

387
25:00.800 --> 25:03.760
It helps with muscles and reduces injuries.

388
25:04.280 --> 25:07.080
And it makes our hearts race like when we fall in love at first sight.

389
25:07.840 --> 25:10.040
You want me to soak in an ice bath?

390
25:10.640 --> 25:12.200
I've never done this.

391
25:12.280 --> 25:13.960
Won't I die from shock?

392
25:15.520 --> 25:18.480
If you could die from this, plenty of people would've died before you.

393
25:18.560 --> 25:20.320
This won't kill you.

394
25:20.920 --> 25:23.040
Anything you've never done, try it all.

395
25:36.920 --> 25:39.080
How do you feel? Is your heart racing?

396
25:40.480 --> 25:41.800
My heart's about to stop instead.

397
25:42.400 --> 25:43.240
You got this.

398
25:54.000 --> 25:56.120
This is the date you planned?

399
25:56.760 --> 25:59.040
Where's your sense of romance?

400
25:59.120 --> 26:01.880
This is a date. We're up this high.

401
26:01.960 --> 26:03.840
There's no way your heart won't race.

402
26:03.920 --> 26:05.720
Your heart rate graph will spike,

403
26:05.800 --> 26:07.600
and maybe the ghost will finally come haunt us.

404
26:09.040 --> 26:10.280
Let me see.

405
26:24.760 --> 26:26.560
-Are we starting now? -Yeah.

406
26:41.160 --> 26:43.400
Vann, I can't do this.

407
26:44.040 --> 26:45.240
It's too high.

408
26:50.360 --> 26:52.360
Trust me.

409
26:52.440 --> 26:53.680
I won't let you fall.

410
27:01.760 --> 27:03.160
Thank you so much.

411
27:05.200 --> 27:06.360
Vann!

412
27:06.960 --> 27:08.120
Wait!

413
27:14.320 --> 27:15.800
That was so much fun.

414
27:15.880 --> 27:17.400
I didn't think I could climb it.

415
27:22.520 --> 27:24.320
See? Just like that.

416
27:24.400 --> 27:26.080
Your heart really is racing.

417
27:31.280 --> 27:32.280
Let's get up.

418
27:35.280 --> 27:36.280
Up.

419
27:39.960 --> 27:41.600
I'm hungry.

420
27:41.680 --> 27:44.280
Is there anything I can eat that'll make my heart race?

421
27:44.360 --> 27:45.640
Sure.

422
27:45.720 --> 27:48.040
I guarantee your heart will burst right out of your chest.

423
27:48.120 --> 27:50.560
Come on. I'll take you there.

424
27:55.800 --> 27:57.000
Raw buffalo larb!

425
27:57.600 --> 28:00.760
It's so hard to find food from my hometown.

426
28:00.840 --> 28:03.400
But how did you find this place?

427
28:03.480 --> 28:05.560
I looked up your family history.

428
28:05.640 --> 28:07.920
You're from an old family in Lamphun.

429
28:08.000 --> 28:09.200
I thought this place would suit you.

430
28:09.280 --> 28:12.200
So I asked Linda to call the owner and bump you up the waitlist.

431
28:13.760 --> 28:14.600
Try it.

432
28:15.960 --> 28:17.480
Then I won't hold back.

433
28:20.720 --> 28:22.040
You should eat with me.

434
29:03.040 --> 29:05.480
You're working for me. How could I let you pay?

435
29:06.160 --> 29:07.400
I'm not here to work.

436
29:07.480 --> 29:09.080
I'm here on a date today.

437
29:10.880 --> 29:13.560
Hey, is that your ex?

438
29:17.320 --> 29:18.160
Done.

439
29:19.440 --> 29:20.600
Keep the change.

440
29:21.440 --> 29:23.800
You paid by QR code, so there isn't any change.

441
29:36.800 --> 29:38.240
What do you think of this bracelet?

442
29:38.320 --> 29:39.480
Is it pretty?

443
29:40.440 --> 29:41.720
It's well-crafted.

444
29:42.440 --> 29:44.160
Hey, be honest.

445
29:46.400 --> 29:47.480
I'd say it's pretty.

446
29:47.560 --> 29:49.280
If it were ugly, I'd tell you.

447
29:52.000 --> 29:53.880
Do you like wearing silver because you're from the North?

448
29:55.160 --> 29:58.040
Yeah, but my family is next-level Yong people.

449
29:58.120 --> 29:59.680
As for worshipping ancestral spirits,

450
29:59.760 --> 30:01.720
it's like the Chinese Ghost Festival

451
30:01.800 --> 30:03.440
or how we Thais worship our ancestors.

452
30:03.520 --> 30:05.720
The ancestral spirits help ward off bad things.

453
30:05.800 --> 30:07.920
They help keep misfortune away from their descendants.

454
30:18.040 --> 30:19.120
What's special about this necklace?

455
30:19.200 --> 30:21.240
This looks like Kan's.

456
30:22.480 --> 30:23.520
My boyfriend.

457
30:25.880 --> 30:27.240
That coward?

458
30:27.320 --> 30:29.400
Hey, don't talk about him like that.

459
30:30.080 --> 30:31.640
He didn't mean to run away from me.

460
30:31.720 --> 30:33.360
He was running from the ghost.

461
30:34.440 --> 30:36.800
I think your ex might be a bad guy.

462
30:36.880 --> 30:38.360
That's why the ghost chased him away.

463
30:41.160 --> 30:42.720
Kan is sweet.

464
30:43.360 --> 30:44.560
He was really good to me.

465
30:45.240 --> 30:46.760
If we can sort out the ghost problem,

466
30:46.840 --> 30:49.440
I'd like to ask Kan to get back together.

467
30:50.440 --> 30:52.280
I don't know if I'll still have a chance.

468
31:38.640 --> 31:41.040
Vann, did you buy me the bracelet?

469
31:42.600 --> 31:43.920
Why are you confused?

470
31:44.000 --> 31:45.800
You wanted it, so I bought it for you.

471
31:48.840 --> 31:49.800
You bought me something.

472
31:49.880 --> 31:52.400
Is that included in the organic date package too?

473
31:54.880 --> 31:57.640
What if I wear it and only think of you?

474
31:58.440 --> 31:59.280
What am I supposed to do?

475
32:09.720 --> 32:10.800
I don't mind.

476
32:10.880 --> 32:12.720
It's good if you think of me instead of Kan.

477
32:13.400 --> 32:14.280
What?

478
32:14.880 --> 32:16.080
What do you mean?

479
32:17.120 --> 32:19.000
I know I'm no love expert,

480
32:19.720 --> 32:20.880
but I think

481
32:20.960 --> 32:22.320
loving each other

482
32:22.400 --> 32:23.920
means supporting each other always.

483
32:24.840 --> 32:26.320
So if we love each other,

484
32:26.960 --> 32:28.640
no matter what problems you face,

485
32:29.240 --> 32:30.600
I'll never run away

486
32:30.680 --> 32:32.080
and leave you alone.

487
32:34.440 --> 32:35.680
From now on, if you're sad,

488
32:35.760 --> 32:37.120
look at this bracelet

489
32:37.720 --> 32:39.320
and think of me instead.

490
32:39.960 --> 32:41.360
You don't have to think of anyone else.

491
32:42.800 --> 32:43.840
Do you understand?

492
32:55.640 --> 32:56.800
Thank you.

493
32:59.600 --> 33:00.440
‎Of course.

494
33:10.840 --> 33:11.640
‎VANN

495
33:11.720 --> 33:13.440
Is the bracelet I gave you comfortable to wear?

496
33:19.000 --> 33:21.560
No, my hand gets swollen and itchy when I wear it.

497
33:21.640 --> 33:22.640
Is it fake silver?

498
33:23.400 --> 33:24.440
It's real silver.

499
33:24.520 --> 33:26.400
It's premium, just like the person who gave it to you.

500
33:34.440 --> 33:36.440
It's Friday. Buy me a beer.

501
33:36.960 --> 33:39.200
Whoever invites the other person pays.

502
33:39.280 --> 33:40.320
You said it yourself, and you forgot.

503
33:43.800 --> 33:46.840
Fine, I'll pay. Will you come meet me?

504
34:03.680 --> 34:06.360
I want to see you, but I'm not done with work yet.

505
34:06.440 --> 34:08.639
Can I call you instead?

506
34:09.639 --> 34:12.480
Hello, Vann. What are you doing?

507
34:12.560 --> 34:14.520
I'm in my room. Where else would I be?

508
34:15.120 --> 34:16.360
Where are you?

509
34:25.960 --> 34:28.440
-Let's take a break. -Hot sausages are here.

510
34:28.520 --> 34:30.560
-They look so good. -Ladies first.

511
34:30.639 --> 34:32.440
-Thank you. -Okay.

512
34:32.520 --> 34:34.600
-I'll have one too. -Thank you.

513
34:34.679 --> 34:36.520
-So damn lucky. A guy's cooking for me. -Here.

514
34:36.600 --> 34:38.440
-Talay, want one? -Thanks.

515
34:38.520 --> 34:39.760
You gave me a whole one.

516
34:39.840 --> 34:41.199
Tell me.

517
34:41.280 --> 34:42.719
Do you guys think he's acting normal?

518
34:44.679 --> 34:46.000
I've never seen this side of him.

519
34:46.679 --> 34:48.560
Maybe he's ordering a new dinosaur figure.

520
34:49.920 --> 34:52.440
Vann, are you this happy while working these days?

521
34:52.520 --> 34:54.199
-Exactly. -Yeah.

522
34:54.280 --> 34:57.040
You usually look so dead inside when talking to clients.

523
34:57.120 --> 34:58.600
What's gotten into you, Vann?

524
34:58.680 --> 35:01.040
I'm discussing a million-baht deal.

525
35:01.120 --> 35:03.320
-Don't bother me. -Yeah, let's leave him alone.

526
35:03.400 --> 35:04.480
Let's just eat.

527
35:07.800 --> 35:08.680
Talay.

528
35:08.760 --> 35:09.680
-What? -So good.

529
35:09.760 --> 35:10.920
Can I borrow your car?

530
35:13.400 --> 35:14.520
Just get a ride.

531
35:14.600 --> 35:15.640
Why do you need my car?

532
35:16.280 --> 35:17.920
I don't want my hair getting all messed up.

533
35:18.000 --> 35:18.920
I'll drive your car.

534
35:19.520 --> 35:21.280
Now he's obsessed with looking good.

535
35:21.360 --> 35:22.520
No.

536
35:22.600 --> 35:24.520
Linda said I'm the youngest.

537
35:24.600 --> 35:26.280
Aren't you guys supposed to take care of me?

538
35:28.120 --> 35:29.160
I'm borrowing your car.

539
35:32.400 --> 35:33.280
Fine.

540
35:35.080 --> 35:36.360
Drive it carefully.

541
35:42.920 --> 35:44.880
Vann, aren't you eating?

542
35:44.960 --> 35:47.520
-No. You guys eat. I'm leaving. -Hey!

543
35:50.840 --> 35:52.200
I didn't mean to do that.

544
35:53.080 --> 35:55.040
If that's all you're going to say, just go.

545
35:55.120 --> 35:56.640
Just go. Go.

546
35:56.720 --> 35:58.000
Hear me out first.

547
35:58.080 --> 35:59.440
-What else do you want me to hear? -Rak.

548
36:03.000 --> 36:04.840
Rak, hold this for a second.

549
36:07.320 --> 36:08.720
Wait, Rakkhun.

550
36:08.800 --> 36:09.800
Rak.

551
36:10.600 --> 36:11.440
Just a second, Rak.

552
36:13.000 --> 36:14.760
Can you stay and talk to me for a second?

553
36:15.520 --> 36:16.520
What is it?

554
36:17.240 --> 36:18.400
Well…

555
36:19.080 --> 36:20.960
That night, I was just shocked.

556
36:23.120 --> 36:24.120
It's okay.

557
36:24.800 --> 36:26.760
Anyone would be shocked by something like that.

558
36:26.840 --> 36:28.160
It's normal.

559
36:28.240 --> 36:29.160
I understand.

560
36:30.400 --> 36:32.720
Thanks so much for understanding me.

561
36:36.360 --> 36:37.440
Well…

562
36:41.480 --> 36:42.640
I…

563
36:43.280 --> 36:45.400
I didn't want to break up with you.

564
36:47.200 --> 36:49.880
It was just a small mishap at the time.

565
36:52.040 --> 36:53.760
Right now, technically…

566
36:54.440 --> 36:55.840
we're still together, right?

567
37:00.480 --> 37:01.960
Well…

568
37:03.840 --> 37:05.480
You don't want to be with me anymore?

569
37:07.120 --> 37:08.480
It's not that.

570
37:09.320 --> 37:10.400
Well…

571
37:21.600 --> 37:23.880
How much longer are you going to make me wait? I want to go home.

572
37:25.400 --> 37:27.720
My brother is here to pick me up.

573
37:27.800 --> 37:29.600
I'll tell you once I have an answer.

574
37:38.040 --> 37:39.240
Didn't you say you couldn't pick me up?

575
37:39.320 --> 37:42.120
Didn't you tell me yesterday you had no one to help you with your model?

576
37:42.200 --> 37:43.480
I'll help you today.

577
37:43.560 --> 37:46.520
I can build it myself.

578
37:46.600 --> 37:48.480
I can stay with my friend another night. It's fine.

579
37:48.560 --> 37:50.720
It's fine. Let's go.

580
38:12.880 --> 38:13.800
Hurry up and eat.

581
38:13.880 --> 38:15.800
Your hands are shaking from hunger. You almost cut yourself.

582
38:17.440 --> 38:18.920
I'm not eating. I'm in a hurry.

583
38:20.440 --> 38:22.440
You said you'd help me with my model.

584
38:23.400 --> 38:25.040
If you lied to me today,

585
38:25.560 --> 38:27.320
I'll tell Linda.

586
38:28.600 --> 38:29.480
I don't care.

587
38:30.200 --> 38:32.280
If you won't eat, I won't help you.

588
38:42.560 --> 38:43.960
Fine, I'll eat.

589
38:55.000 --> 38:56.960
You'll definitely get your work done.

590
38:57.040 --> 38:58.920
I don't make promises I can't keep.

591
39:17.360 --> 39:18.640
I'm going to wash my hands.

592
39:19.440 --> 39:20.440
Vann.

593
39:30.520 --> 39:31.920
Kan came to talk to me.

594
39:33.360 --> 39:36.040
He apologized and said he was just shocked back then.

595
39:36.800 --> 39:38.520
And he also told me

596
39:38.600 --> 39:39.920
he still loves me.

597
39:40.520 --> 39:41.960
What do you think I should do?

598
39:44.960 --> 39:47.240
You want to get back together with him, don't you?

599
39:50.040 --> 39:51.680
But if I get back together with him,

600
39:51.760 --> 39:54.720
I don't know if he'll leave me again when he sees the ghost.

601
39:55.360 --> 39:57.680
Then hurry up and finish the model for your professor,

602
39:58.280 --> 40:00.080
so we can get back to focusing on the ghost-hunting mission,

603
40:00.680 --> 40:02.200
and I can get my job done sooner.

604
40:02.800 --> 40:04.520
Then, you can get back together with him.

605
40:04.600 --> 40:05.600
Sound good?

606
40:06.840 --> 40:08.680
I hope that's how it turns out.

607
40:10.320 --> 40:11.160
Hurry up and do it.

608
40:11.880 --> 40:12.920
-Go on. -I am.

609
40:39.560 --> 40:42.040
Don't you have to be on campus to build your model tonight?

610
40:42.120 --> 40:43.520
Can I come see you?

611
40:45.520 --> 40:48.280
That's okay. I want to do it alone.

612
41:19.400 --> 41:21.360
If you can't stay up, go to sleep first.

613
41:21.440 --> 41:22.560
I'll do the rest.

614
41:24.000 --> 41:25.520
You're even better at it than me.

615
41:26.520 --> 41:28.280
Didn't you say you studied engineering?

616
41:29.480 --> 41:32.360
Some things, you're just born with.

617
41:32.440 --> 41:33.680
It's called talent.

618
41:34.320 --> 41:36.840
Next time you have another model to build, just hire me

619
41:37.480 --> 41:38.840
so you won't have to work so hard.

620
41:39.760 --> 41:41.280
I'm sleepy.

621
41:41.360 --> 41:42.600
I can't stay awake anymore.

622
41:50.840 --> 41:51.840
Go to sleep.

623
42:03.920 --> 42:05.280
Get some sleep.

624
42:05.360 --> 42:06.400
I'll wake you when it's done.

625
42:08.360 --> 42:09.600
Aren't you going to sleep?

626
42:12.400 --> 42:13.640
I stay up late every night anyway.

627
42:17.520 --> 42:18.920
I'm just worried about you.

628
42:20.880 --> 42:22.160
Thanks, Vann.

629
42:23.560 --> 42:25.240
You're really good to me.

630
43:34.120 --> 43:35.240
Do you see it?

631
43:36.560 --> 43:37.960
Is that the ghost?

632
43:39.720 --> 43:41.960
Why are you scared? I'm here.

633
43:43.000 --> 43:44.640
As for the ghost,

634
43:45.560 --> 43:47.080
it should be scared of me.

635
44:02.960 --> 44:04.760
Get ready for a "nice to meet you,"

636
44:04.840 --> 44:05.920
you stupid ghost.

637
44:50.000 --> 44:52.040
-Do you trust me, Rak? -Of course I do.

638
